================================================================================
Third-party software and reference implementations
================================================================================

Hugging Face Candle — https://github.com/huggingface/candle
    Copyright (c) 2023- Hugging Face, Inc. Apache-2.0 / MIT (dual).
    Light is a port of Candle's design: the tensor, op, dtype and model
    surface follow it, and CUDA kernels under kernels/cuda/src/ were written
    against Candle's candle-kernels as the reference.

Hugging Face transformers — https://github.com/huggingface/transformers
    Apache-2.0. The transformer-model ports (Llama, Qwen, Gemma, Phi, Falcon,
    BERT, Whisper, Qwen3-ASR, Mimi, EmbeddingGemma, …) follow its modelling
    code and are verified against it; scripts/verify/ drives it to produce
    the reference numbers in the tests.

llama.cpp / ggml — https://github.com/ggml-org/llama.cpp
    MIT. The GGUF container, the block-quantization formats (Q4_0 … Q8_K)
    and the GGUF tokenizer semantics in gguf/, quant/ and tokenizer/gguf.go
    follow its specification.

Kyutai Moshi — https://github.com/kyutai-labs/moshi
    MIT (code), CC-BY-4.0 (model weights). The Mimi codec and the Moshi
    language model in models/mimi*.go and models/moshi*.go follow its
    Python and Rust (moshi-core) implementations and are verified against
    them.

Google SentencePiece — https://github.com/google/sentencepiece
    Apache-2.0. tokenizer/spm_model.go reads its model protobuf and
    reproduces its unigram segmentation.

NVIDIA CUDA Toolkit, cuBLAS, cuBLASLt and cuDNN are used through their C
APIs under the NVIDIA Software License Agreement; they are not distributed
with this repository.

================================================================================
Test assets
================================================================================

testdata/whisper/*.wav and testdata/mimi/*.wav are resampled copies of the
"Front Center" speaker-test sample distributed with alsa-utils
(https://github.com/alsa-project/alsa-utils, GPL-2.0), used only as a
fixture for speech tests. models/testdata/falcon/* are tiny random-weight
checkpoints generated by scripts/verify/ref_falcon.py for architecture
tests and carry no trained weights.

Model weights are never stored in this repository: tests download them
from the Hugging Face Hub under each model's own license.
